WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.090
The UN says urban areas consume
75 per cent of the world's energy,

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.730
and produce 75 per cent of
its greenhouse gas emissions.

3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.490
Freiburg, Germany.

4
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:17.050
In Vauban, a former army barracks,
residential streets have no public parking.

5
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.270
Building there must be low-energy, and
some houses produce more energy than they

6
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.290
use.

7
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.670
But Vauban is home to about 5,300 people.

8
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.890
Can eco-cities and smart
cities make a real difference?

9
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.210
Or does it all depend on
national energy supplies?

10
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.410
In this mission, you'll measure
footprints in global hectares,

11
00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:40.770
and compare Vauban with
China's Tianjin Eco-City.

12
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:46.590
Then you'll test smart-city claims, from
Masdar City in Abu Dhabi to Barcelona.

13
00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:52.190
Your mission: evaluate whether eco-cities
and smart cities can make a real difference.
